-- title:
--   From HTo G Ev Sum Is Some False Weight
-- statement:
--   **Bipartite expectations respect the residual G-hat partition.** Let $\rho$ be a bipartite state, let $A$ and $S$ be local operators, and fix $x\in\mathbb{F}_q$. With $U_{x,g}$ and $R_x$ denoting the indexed G-hat effects and incomplete-part total, the failure branch satisfies
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{g\,:\,g.\mathrm{isSome}=\mathrm{false}}
--   \operatorname{ev}_{\rho}\!\left((A\otimes I)(I\otimes(SU_{x,g}U_{x,g}))\right)
--   =\operatorname{ev}_{\rho}\!\left((A\otimes I)(I\otimes(SR_x))\right).
--   $$
--
--   This residual expectation identity is paired with the complete-branch identity when the missing slice mass is averaged in the Bernoulli recurrence.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The source declaration is `MIPStarRE.LDT.Pasting.fromHToG_ev_sum_isSome_false_weight`; its Lean statement gives the exact quantifier order and all boundary hypotheses.
